PART 23 — FIVE-LAYER CENTRAL MYSTERY

Connect the new content to the main narrative through five discovery layers.

Layer 1: The World Is Older Than Its History

Recorded history begins long after Aethwyrd's actual formation.

Layer 2: The Gods Are Not the First Beings

Primordial entities existed before the modern gods.

Layer 3: The World Has Been Recreated

Evidence suggests Aethwyrd has experienced previous cycles of destruction and rebirth.

Layer 4: The Status System Is Part of Something Larger

The System is connected to the mechanism governing these world cycles.

Layer 5: The Original Beginning

The ultimate mystery concerns the origin of the first world and the entity responsible for its creation.

Keep these revelations distributed throughout the game.

Do not reveal everything in a single exposition scene.

